cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite the paper it implements (below under
  preferred-citation). If you need to refer to this code specifically, for
  example to a particular release, cite the software entry as well.
title: >-
  Reference implementation of a secure, message-centric air-ground
  communication protocol
abstract: >-
  A research implementation of the protocol specified in Section 3.3 of the
  accompanying paper: a three-message mutually authenticated key agreement
  with explicit confirmation over the transcript, credentials carried in the
  messages and verified against issuer trust anchors, a challenge issued by
  the aircraft binding each command to the report it answers, and transfer of
  control between ground stations requiring no channel between them. Built on
  Ed25519, X25519 and the Ascon family of lightweight primitives.
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: '2026-10-24'
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: 'https://github.com/Erwin-O/Aviation_wireless_communications'
# Fill in once a release has been archived and a DOI minted:
# doi: 10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX
keywords:
  - air-ground communication
  - message-centric security
  - aviation datalink
  - authenticated key exchange
  - lightweight cryptography
  - Ascon
  - formal verification
  - unmanned aerial systems
# This software was written by Erwin Orye alone. The paper it implements has
# four authors; they are listed under preferred-citation below.
# The ProVerif models carried in proverif/ are Frederic Lafitte's work, are
# credited in NOTICE and proverif/README.md, and are not part of the
# implementation.
